Z||000000||aleroboy||12-12-2001||04:48 PM||||hi i'm new here and I'm going to get a fiero in the summer to start building.<BR>first which is better the 87 or 88 gt?<BR>also my friend and i think it would be cool to have the doors open up like a lamborginni.<BR>do any places offer this?<BR>what palces offer stuff for the body?<BR>I seen a fiero her in town that had some really cool looking side scoops. any help would be great!!||||reg||4
Z||000001||WampusCat||12-12-2001||05:38 PM||||Welcome to the forum!  The 88 vs older models is an ongoing debate.  Basically, the 88 has upgraded suspension and brakes compared to other years but parts and cars are generally cheaper/more available for the 87 and earlier.  You can probably find the answers to most of your questions by using the search function, probably in the technical section.  Look just under the white GT with Santa in the upper right part of the screen for the search link.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||12-12-2001||05:40 PM||||Well, that's a pretty broad bunch of requests! First of all, Welcome to the forum.<P>Now to your questions.<P>87 vs. 88?  Well, they are (for the most part) visually the same (I'm assuming that you're speaking of the GT anyway). The 88 does have an upgraded suspension- which stock is technically superior to the stock 87 & eariler suspension.  Although due to the volume of 87 & eariler Fieros... aftermarket parts (including advanced upgraded suspension & brakes) are more abudant than those of the 88s.<P>Lambo doors?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> This is fun topic. I'd suggest running a search (top/right corner of the screen) and searching for "scissor doors" or "lambo doors" (in the technical or tech archives). Someone has been working on developing a kit to do this, but there have not been any completed prototypes as of yet.  (it'd be cool though, wouldn't it?)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mychopped2_1.jpg"> <BR>don't ask...it's just photoshop!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Stuff for the body. Well, that again is rather broad for a question.  There are many suppliers of replacement pontiac & mecham style 1/4 scoops, as well as replacement scoop/windows for the GT-style bodies, (check for Ferrari_Momo's website- I don't have it handy).  Also IRM is a common place to get aftermarket body panels... just have to be patient with shipping times.  Look around... if you seee something specific that you like the looks of, just ask!  Most people will be quick to help you locate the parts/suppliers that you're looking for!<P>Again, welcome... use the search... if still no answers- ask away!<P>------------------<BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 12-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||3.8T Fiero GT||12-12-2001||05:46 PM||||nothing, buy an import instead!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>*Your ASS here*   <IMG SRC="http://www.plaudersmilies.de/rough/zzwhip.gif"> <BR><B>"A 3.8T makes and excellent "RICE" cooker"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||aleroboy||12-12-2001||05:54 PM||||ok I just checked out V8 archie's site<BR>has anyone bought a finale or fino body kit??<BR>what does everyone prefer?<BR>thanks for all the help now time to dig thru past topics!||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||12-12-2001||05:58 PM||||Finale vs. Fino... I'd take the Finale in a second! (Then again, that's just my personal preference).  Archie is by far one of the best Fiero vendors around- he comes amazingly highly recommended.  I've seen both body kits up close, and just prefer the lines of the Finale myself.  <P>Check out David Gageby's Finale on the MFF website: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.mn.org/Cars/Finale/Default.asp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.mn.org/Cars/Finale/Default.asp</A>   He's running a sweet 383 stroker and has an absolutely beautiful car! (although his running a Zumalt conversion instead of an Archie... not my choice!)<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 12-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||aleroboy||12-12-2001||06:20 PM||||good to know that they are good kits!<BR>from what I've seen he also has the best price on it.<BR>I kinda like the front of the fino. but with either one people will be asking what it is!<BR>I want to use a 3400sfi with a turbo to power the car. I know quite a bit about the 60 deg V6 engine. one more question how much does a stock fiero weigh? I"m having a hard time finding that.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Joe Torma||12-12-2001||07:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by aleroboy:<BR><B>I want to use a 3400sfi with a turbo to power the car. I know quite a bit about the 60 deg V6 engine. one more question how much does a stock fiero weigh? I"m having a hard time finding that.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm one of 2 here using the 3400SFI.  Not turbo though.  I went with an aftermarket engine control system...OBDII sux.<P>Fiero weight...most are around 2750.<BR>The 3400 is a bit lighter than the stock 2.8.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/3400_3.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
